<%# The archive, opened from the middle of the screen.

    A dialog rather than a column: a hit is a place in another conversation, and
    its sentence needs the width of the page to be worth reading. It is a real
    <dialog>, so the browser supplies the top layer, the focus trap, escape to
    close and an inert page behind it.

    The field never moves; only the list under it scrolls. The initial hint is
    what the pane says before the first keystroke asks anything — the first
    answer replaces it, which is why the empty state is markup here rather than
    a branch in the fragment. -%>
<dialog id="search-dialog" class="search-dialog" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.search.label")) %>">
  <div class="search-top">
    <input class="search-input" type="search" name="q" autocomplete="off"
           placeholder="<%= h(I18n.t("web.search.placeholder")) %>" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.search.label")) %>"
           hx-get="/search<%= h(token_query) %>"
           hx-trigger="input changed delay:220ms, search"
           hx-target="#search-results"
           hx-swap="innerHTML">
    <button class="search-close" type="button" data-search-close title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.search.close")) %>">esc</button>
  </div>
  <div id="search-results" class="search-results-pane" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="search-hint"><%= h(I18n.t("web.search.hint")) %></p>
  </div>
</dialog>
